{"ts": "2026-09-27T15:53:44+00:00", "t": 1790524424.7212055, "model": "jev-1.13.0", "qhash": "991cac0aed", "stage": "step", "tool": "execute_command", "target": "python -c \"\nimport time\nimport app.ratelimit as ratelimit\n\n# Simulate the mutant: t >= cutoff (keep timestamps AT the boundary)\n# Test: inject timestamps at now-60, then call is_rate_limited\n# With t > cutoff: now-60 > now_func-60 is False (pruned)\n# With t >= cutoff: now-60 >= now_func-60 is False (also pruned because now_func > test_now)\n# So the boundary test can't distinguish them via time.monotonic() drift\n\n# The only way: mock time.monotonic\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\n\nratelimit._attempts.pop('test', None)\nfake_now = 1000.0\n# Inject 5 timestamps at exactly fake_now - 60\nratelimit._attempts['test'] = [fake_now - 60.0] * 5\n\n# With current code (t > cutoff): cutoff = fake_now - 60 = 940.0\n# timestamps are [940.0, 940.0, ...]; 940.0 > 940.0 is False -> all pruned -> allowed\nwith patch('app.ratelimit.time') as mock_time:\n    mock_time.monotonic.return_value = fake_now\n    result = ratelimit.is_rate_limited('test')\n    print(f'With t>cutoff (correct code): {result}')  # should be False\n\n# Now simulate mutant: t >= cutoff\n# timestamps are [940.0, ...]; 940.0 >= 940.0 is True -> kept -> len=5 -> blocked\nimport app.ratelimit as rl2\nrl2._attempts['test2'] = [fake_now - 60.0] * 5\n# Patch the condition manually\nimport types\ndef patched_is_rate_limited(user):\n    now = fake_now\n    cutoff = now - 60\n    timestamps = rl2._attempts.get(user)\n    if timestamps is None:\n        timestamps = []\n        rl2._attempts[user] = timestamps\n    timestamps[:] = [t for t in timestamps if t >= cutoff]  # mutant\n    if len(timestamps) >= 5:\n        return True\n    timestamps.append(now)\n    return False\n\nresult_mutant = patched_is_rate_limited('test2')\nprint(f'With t>=cutoff (mutant): {result_mutant}')  # should be True\n\"\n", "action": "block", "note": "no declared intent"}
